# This setup's live file. 192.168.4.32 is the LAN address of the server host
# that runs piwii's web server, reserved in the router. For another setup,
# start from piwii.exports.example instead.
#
# piwii: staging area where finished games land before the Pi syncs them onto
# the game drive. Only the server host (192.168.4.32) may mount it. People add games
# through the piwii web server, never by mounting this directly.
# all_squash maps the client to admin (1000) so files stay owned by admin.
# crossmnt lets the server host see the status/ tmpfs mounted inside staging.
/srv/piwii/staging 192.168.4.32(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,all_squash,anonuid=1000,anongid=1000,crossmnt)
# status/ is a RAM-only tmpfs (see srv-piwii-staging-status.mount). tmpfs has
# no stable filesystem ID, so it needs an explicit fsid. Read-only: the
# web server only reads status.
/srv/piwii/staging/status 192.168.4.32(ro,sync,no_subtree_check,all_squash,anonuid=1000,anongid=1000,fsid=7701)
